# tools/sbom/module_info_to_spdx.rb.
---
directory: src
license: MIT
name: SparX-III Unmanaged switch firmware
description: 8051 firmware for the Microchip SparX-III (Luton26) unmanaged switches (VSC5609EV, VSC5610EV-UN)
source: https://github.com/microchip-ung/SparX-III_Unmanaged
# 'git' = the revision being described ('git describe --tags'), so this stays
# right without a hand-edit per release.
version: git
attribution_file: COPYING
---
# I2C driver header carrying the eCos license header rather than MIT. Included
# by main.c, i2c_h.c, clihnd.c and phytsk.c, so it is compiled into every image.
files: src/main/i2c_h.h
license: GPL-2.0-or-later WITH eCos-exception-2.0
name: VCore-III I2C driver header
description: I2C driver interface for the VCore-III CPU, under the eCos license
# Microchip's own driver code, released under the eCos license - not a copy of
# upstream eCos, so no download location or purl is claimed for it.
source: Microchip Technology Inc. (eCos license)
attribution: |
  This file is part of eCos, the Embedded Configurable Operating System.
  Copyright (C) 2005, 2006 Free Software Foundation, Inc.

  eCos is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify it under
  the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by the Free
  Software Foundation; either version 2 or (at your option) any later
  version.

  As a special exception, if other files instantiate templates or use
  macros or inline functions from this file, or you compile this file
  and link it with other works to produce a work based on this file,
  this file does not by itself cause the resulting work to be covered by
  the GNU General Public License. However the source code for this file
  must still be made available in accordance with section (3) of the GNU
  General Public License v2.
---
# Keil's STARTUP.A51 template, adapted for Luton26. Copied out of the Keil C51
# installation into the repo, so it ships in the source and is linked into
# every image.
files: src/main/startup.a51
license: Keil
name: Keil C51 startup code
description: 8051 reset/startup code (STARTUP.A51) from the Keil C51 compiler package
source: Keil Elektronik GmbH and Keil Software, Inc.
attribution: |
  This file is part of the C51 Compiler package
  Copyright (c) 1988-2002 Keil Elektronik GmbH and Keil Software, Inc.

  Distributed under the terms of the Keil C51 development tools license
  agreement, which covers use of the startup code in applications built with
  the Keil tools.
---
# The compiler/linker the images are built with (prj/luton26u.uvproj).
# Proprietary and NOT in this repo: category Toolchain makes it BUILD_TOOL_OF
# the release and each image, without being contained in the release.
placeholder: true
license: Keil
name: Keil C51 / uVision (MCS-51)
description: Keil C51 compiler, A51 assembler, BL51 linker and OH51 hex converter
source: https://www.keil.arm.com/
category: Toolchain
attribution: |
  Copyright (c) Arm Limited (Keil)

  Proprietary; licensed separately to each developer and not distributed with
  this repository.
